MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- new pure module silhouette.rs: a Silhouette is a box Part composition plus
  the derived ground radius and the unit flag; nine hand-tuned specs keyed by
  the bundle kind name (worker+tool, rifleman+rifle, raider buggy, Guardian
  hull/treads/turret/barrel, CC tower, barracks flag, depot crate stack,
  turret pedestal, amber ore crystals) with the capability-shape fallback
  (Resource -> cluster, Footprint -> building, Move -> unit, else plain box)
- part tones (Body/Dark/Light/Steel/Band/Amber) resolve against the team
  palette, so kinds read apart while teams stay obvious; every structure
  carries a team band part (§2.2's banner), every unit keeps the squat cue
- render.rs: build_entity_instances composes parts (offsets rotate with the
  facing — the transposed form matching the shader's mirrored yaw), shadows
  and rings size from the derived radius, death fades shrink the main mass
- main.rs: kind_shapes() resolves via the name table + capability fallback
- 10 new silhouette tests + the render tests re-pinned (unique mesh per kind,
  part counts / vertex counts, above-ground + inside-radius invariants,
  fallback paths, ore amber team-independent)
