--- a/AI-Handoff.md
+++ b/AI-Handoff.md
@@ -986,7 +986,7 @@ existing `ai_host` seam.
 - **The decal instance buffer is ONE shared stream with order-dependent blending**: shadows, the placement ghost, team rings, and selection rings share the 1024-instance buffer, drawn as `[shadows+ghost]` on the quad vertices and `[team rings + selection rings]` on the ring vertices. Alpha blending paints in buffer order — the selection ring must extend AFTER the team rings so green reads over the owner color. Capacity trimming preserves whole groups; if you add a decal group, decide its blend order explicitly and keep the range arithmetic (`shadow_count + ghost_count ..`) exact.
 - **Minimap markers paint over fog — the entity list must stay the fog-filtered view.** `paint_minimap_markers` (pure, tested) draws AFTER the fog shading with no per-entity fog check; it is honest only because `main.rs` hands it the PlayerView's entities (what the player may see). Feeding it a full snapshot would draw hidden entities onto hidden tiles. The marker shapes are per-role: units 1 tile (own blue / enemy orange), buildings a solid 2×2 block, neutral ore a 3×3 amber diamond — color AND shape AND size, per the plan's "distinct markers, buildings visibly larger".
 - **`Silhouette` is not `Copy` — spec lookups clone, the fallback is capability-shaped.** The renderer's `kind_specs` are indexed by `KindId`; a miss falls to `fallback_shape()` (the plain unit box) via `.cloned().unwrap_or_else(...)`. The kind→shape mapping is resolved ONCE at startup in `main.rs::kind_shapes`: the name table (`silhouette::named`) is exact-match on the bundle's kind ids, and unknown names fall through `capability_fallback` (Resource → cluster, Attack+Footprint w/o Move → turret, Footprint → building, Move → unit). A content kind-id rename therefore silently changes which silhouette a kind gets — the DEBT-016 tripwire — while the shape-only fallback keeps rendering something sane.
-- **M10.2 Phase 2 deliberately left the exit's screenshot half to the owner**: the machine half of "a stranger identifies command center, worker, and tank" ran (Xvfb smoke + the pure geometry tests); the owner opted for a text-only delivery (A-104 — no PNGs in the delivery folder), so the human eyeball pass IS their re-test.
+- **M10.2 Phase 2's exit test: the machine half ran on Xvfb, the eyeball half is the owner's re-test** (A-104 — the owner opted for a text-only delivery, no PNGs in the delivery folder). What Xvfb+llvmpipe verified: CC/worker/ore identified on sight via the new silhouettes, hover tooltips with owner tags (Worker/yours, Ore Node/neutral, Command Center/yours), the bigger always-on selected health bar, selection brackets + the worker build panel, the minimap markers. The pass caught a live miss — the CC's tower mass fell outside the fixed hover radius — fixed by `pick_visible_entity_sized` (footprint-scaled reach; the fixed-radius API is gone, callers supply the extra). The Guardian was never on camera (the start force fields none); its silhouette is test-pinned only.
 
